I just installed OpenGD77 on a pair of MD-9600 radios I picked up cheap (v2.1 &amp; v5.0) with no hitches and to my recollection, the process was no different from when I first came across this firmware a couple of years ago. I've installed it on numerous TYT &amp; Baofeng radios for myself and friends and like you say, it's a little confusing for a first-timer. But each time, I try out the radio first and am absolutely shocked at how awful the stock firmware is on these things! I considered leaving one of the MD-9600 stock, but after a few hours of using it that plan got a big NOPE!!  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> <br><br>Do you recall what DMR filtering settings you were using with OpenGD77? Whenever I experience this issue, I eventually realize I've inadvertently changed to the wrong filter. Do you experience the issue on repeaters, a hotspot or both? I'd ask if you're sure you're using the right donor firmware but I believe the CPS would tell you if you're not.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4063">KC6WOG</a> — Mon May 19, 2025 10:31 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
